    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16139" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσελγ-αίνω</span></b> , impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠσέλγαινον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					21.31
				</span></i>
			: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσελγᾰνῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					24.143
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσελγᾶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					52.31
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, pf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠσέλγημαι</span> (v. infr.): plpf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠσέλγητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					17.5.6
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσελγής,</span>
			<i>behave licentiously,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				190c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴς τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					54.5
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, of acts, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ εἰς ἐμὲ ἠσελγημένα</span>”
				<i>outrageous acts,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					21.19
				</span></i>
			.</div>
